{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790960695,"nonce":"77eZ0+pYFJtC6wFNayfNZa79B+8=","title":"a throw from a native primitive aborts instead of reaching the Haxe catch","message":"A primitive that raises through `hl_throw` (hlwgpu's carriers do, for every backend error x-idl's generated code reports) does not unwind to the Haxe `try`/`catch` around the call. Ash prints `hlp_throw called without active trap; aborting` (std/src/error.rs) and the Haxe code after the call runs as if nothing was thrown.\n\nReproducer, with an xwindow HashLink adapter as xwindow.hdll:\n\n    try {\n        w.setCursorImage(haxe.io.Bytes.alloc(3), 2, 2, 0, 0); // backend raises: not 2x2 RGBA\n        trace(\"short cursor taken\");\n    } catch (e:Dynamic) {\n        trace(\"short cursor refused: \" + e);\n    }\n\nprints the abort message, then `short cursor taken`. Under stock HashLink a native `hl_throw` is caught by the enclosing trap.","files":null}]}